.TH WB\-REVISION 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-revision \- print the version, the revision and its manifest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR revision [\-q | \-\-quiet]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Print the version of the package, the hash of its revision and the manifest: the hash of every file the revision holds. Writes nothing.
.PP
\-q (\-\-quiet) is taken and changes nothing: what it prints is what a script reads.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Taken, and changes nothing: what the command prints is what a script reads.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
It is printed.
.TP
.B 1
The manifest could not be made.
.TP
.B 2
It was given a word: it takes none.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wb (1) ,
.BR wb\-check (1) ,
.BR wb\-upgrade (1)
